You have two data frames in R: `pólizas` (issued policies) and `siniestros` (recorded claims).
Write the R code (using `dplyr`) to produce a summary table by segment with the following metrics:
• Number of policies and total exposure
• Number of claims and total claim amount
• Claim frequency (claims/policies)
• Average severity per claim
• Estimated pure risk premium (frequency × severity)
• Loss ratio, assuming an average premium per policy of $800,000
